WebGL for pages through the host browser's WebGL.

Each page context draws through a WebGL context of the host, on an
OffscreenCanvas in the engine thread. WebCore's shared WebGL code is kept; its
ANGLE entry points resolve to a shim over Emscripten's GL functions, so no
ANGLE library is built. WebGL is allowed without accelerated compositing (the
canvas paints from its drawing buffer), and WEBGL_debug_renderer_info reports
the host's GPU.

